  "final_message": "<think>Interesting! The submit DID reach the root and the form's React onSubmit handler DID fire (FETCH /api/tracks appeared). Note the order of the log: \"FETCH /api/tracks\" came before \"submit reached root\" \u2014 that's because my root listener was added after React's, and React's handler ran first (React's listener was attached first). So React's onSubmit works.\n\nSo the earlier interaction test failed for a different reason! In the interaction test, the fetch stub for POST /api/tracks checked `options.headers.Authorization`... wait no, in interact.mjs the POST handler doesn't check auth. Hmm.\n\nWait, in interact.mjs, the POST /api/tracks branch: I check `if (url === \"/api/tracks\" && method === \"POST\")`. But the URL check order: the first branch is `if (url.startsWith(\"/api/tracks?\") || url === \"/api/tracks\")` \u2014 that catches url === \"/api/tracks\" for ALL methods, including POST! So the POST was handled by the GET branch and returned an empty list. That's the bug in my test, not the app.\n\nLet me fix the order in interact.mjs: check the POST method first.\n\nAlso `state.tracks` never got the new track \u2192 no delete button \u2192 the click on null.\n\nLet me fix and re-run.</think>\n\n",
